Z||000000||Luperman||12-26-1999||03:26 AM||||anyone know where the wires that plug into the ac compressor clutch go to I can seem to locate the ones on my 86 SE V-6 . Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||dogtired||12-26-1999||04:34 AM||||I am a little confused with your post?<BR>Well  I am lets just say a little confused most of the time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Not sure which end of the wire you are speaking? The connector that goes to the clutch, is on the front side of the compressor directly above the pulley, If you look real hard with a flashlight down beside the battery I think you can see it from the top, right beside the belt. Real close to the pulley, moving parts. BE CAREFUL!  There is also a single wire on the tail end of the compressor, I think a ground wire.<BR>Hope this helps, and this is what you were looking for?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now if you are wanting to know from the clutch connector to the wire bundle, ???<BR>||||reg||6
